{"version" 2 "boxes" [{"id" "imgui_vr_panel" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "imgui_vr_renderer"} "name" "imgui vr panel" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [300.0 140.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "imgui_vr_panel_code_.kt" "inline" "/*\nImGui as a VR panel.\n\nImGuiVrPanelDemo wires the whole pipeline: an ImGuiRenderToTexture drawn into an RTT,\ntextured onto a world-space ImGuiPanel quad, rendered once per eye by\nSideBySideStereoTarget, packed side-by-side, and blitted to the window. The panel is\ninteractive: the mock controller (here driven by the mouse) casts a ray, the hit is\nconverted to panel UV, and injected into ImGui.\n\nMove the mouse to aim the ray; left-click to press.\nFor a custom hand-attached panel, use the ImGuiPanel construction and registration in\nafield.examples.four.ImGuiVrPanelDemo.build. Its private panel is not exposed by demo.\n*/\nimport afield.examples.four.ImGuiVrPanelDemo\n\nval sbs = SideBySideStereoTarget(renderer)\nval demo = ImGuiVrPanelDemo(renderer.window, renderer, sbs)\ndemo.build()\n\n// Mouse drives the mock controller ray on the desktop (a real controller drives it in XR).\nsbs.enableMouseController(distanceMeters = 0.001f)\n\nprintln(\"imgui vr panel ready — move the mouse to aim the ray, click to press\")\n"}}} {"id" "imgui_vr_renderer" "properties" {"children" #{#afield/box "imgui_vr_panel"} "parents" #{#afield/box "root"} "name" "window + renderer" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 40.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "imgui_vr_renderer_code_.kt" "inline" "import afield.graphics.vulkan.util.Options\n\nprop<Window>(window)\nprop<Renderer>(renderer)\n\nOptions.enableHDR = false\n\nonce.renderer {\n    window = Window(\"ImGui VR panel\")\n    Renderer(window)\n}\n\nprintln(\"imgui vr renderer ready\")\nstart(renderer::run)\n"}}}] "persistentProperties" ["frame" "name" "code" "code_language" "contents_language" "default_property" 